      "concepts": [
        "ProfitLoss"
      ],
      "note": "NetIncomeLoss is the PARENT-attributable figure in US-GAAP, not the consolidated total. Using it as a fallback made consolidated income equal parent income while a noncontrolling interest was reported separately (NWL 2018-Q2: parent 185.0, noncontrolling 3.7, \"consolidated\" 185.0). When ProfitLoss is absent the consolidated figure is derived from parent + noncontrolling instead."
